msgid "Magfit WebTools Utility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:5
#: 193dab57a42b46d394e83d78de6dee4c
msgid "Advanced Compass Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:7
#: 456ee5f6f4b148208943b3d08174ae05
msgid "This article provides advanced guidance for how to setup the system compass(es) and advanced compass related features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:11
#: 6e3d8711c93940c781052603145be94c
msgid "Users who have only internal compasses or an external compass using a UBlox GPS + compass combination,such as :ref:`UBlox GPS + Compass Module <common-installing-3dr-ublox-gps-compass-module>`, and have mounted it in the default orientation can usually perform a simple \"Onboard Calibration\" as described in :ref:`Compass Calibration <common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:14
#: 3814c1cbe6f14388acb3c39be8e3444c
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:16
#: 5b7807c3eeca493f96fc73c59caa2645
msgid "Accurately setting up the compass is critical because it is the primary source of heading information. Without an accurate heading the vehicle will not move in the correct direction in autopilot modes (i.e. AUTO, LOITER, PosHold, RTL, etc). This can lead to circling (aka \"toiletbowling\") or fly-aways."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:22
#: 69be7c38aca64bd1bdd8b7d4aeadf339
msgid "ArduPilot allows multiple compasses to be connected, but only three are used at one time. And usually, only the primary compass is used, unless there are consistency problems with its readings versus other compasses and/or other sensors. In this case, the autopilot will automatically determine which of the first three compasses to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:24
#: b7ed5307ebb94495967f9c9cf2d72d70
msgid "While many autopilots have an internal compass or compasses, many applications will instead use an external compass. This provides more reliable data than an internal compass because of the separation from other electronics. See :ref:`common-autopilots` for details about the specific autopilot to determine how many built-in compasses the autopilot may have, if any."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:28
#: d0ccc9684fdc490a84a59ce1a29db29e
msgid "Most users will only need to  perform the normal :ref:`Compass Calibration<common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner>` but details are also given on the less-used  :ref:`CompassMot <common-compass-setup-advanced_compassmot_compensation_for_interference_from_the_power_wires_escs_and_motors>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:32
#: ea0698e155624cc8be50c30aba7cf086
msgid "Compass Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:34
#: 92c3a960b1654202866e901df4c4fb06
msgid "The *Mission Planner Compass Setup screen* can be found in menu **Setup \\| Mandatory Hardware \\| Compass** in the sidebar. This screen is used for setting compass ordering, priority, calibration, and use. No other settings are required for normal use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:41
#: 462e70332abd4b678ae29a00260514d2
msgid "Mission Planner: Advanced Compass Setup and Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:45
#: c2862d665eea43c8a55cb878abf9684f
msgid "Compass Ordering and Priority"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:47
#: e794049a7b1f4e248da2f7a6dcabd60d
msgid "During boot, ArduPilot automatically detects the compasses present in the system, adds them to a list, and assigns the first three a priority (1-3) linked to their DEV ID (``COMPASS_PRIOx_ID``), according to the order in which they are discovered. This priority determines which compass is used by the EKF lanes. The primary compass (highest priority, 1) will be used by all lanes, and fallback to the next viable compass in the first three priorities, if the primary becomes unhealthy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:49
#: f268d77639e04852b4d1d8c57334715c
msgid "The list of discovered compasses and their priority is maintained across boots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:51
#: 0c0e8af44572410e863a0a9970b5a5cd
msgid "If a user wishes to change to a different compass for one of the three priorities, he can change the ``COMPASS_PRIOx_ID`` to that compass's ``COMPASS_DEV_IDx`` ID value. If a ``COMPASS_PRIOx_ID`` is set to zero, the compasses will be moved up contiguously, in order, to fill that priority slot on the next reboot. This is easily done in Mission Planner with the arrows on the right side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:53
#: 6617ccd8b26142318068a046e7ab7724
msgid "never change a compass's ``COMPASS_DEV_IDx`` ID value manually and then reboot!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:55
#: 73c91838f49b44b3a0c0da07990f7778
msgid "If a previously discovered compass is missing or not detected on boot, and is in one of the three priority positions, a pre-arm failure will occur warning the user. The user will need to either remove the compass from the priority position, or correct the problem in order to prevent the pre-arm failure. Mission Planner provides a button to remove an undetected compass on the above screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:57
#: 0fa931cfe1f643f3ac70b49bbb1f6840
msgid "Compasses not present or detected during a calibration will automatically be removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:60
#: 25bbb10248394f8c996d76e5ea725b35
msgid "Compass Enables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:62
#: bffcabb2b85245058c5a18d4c8b6a9db
msgid "Any one of the first three compasses can be disabled. This would leave only the remaining ones to be used by the autopilot. You may wish to disable any internal compasses if you are consistently seeing the “inconsistent compasses” pre-arm message often and you are sure that the external compass is calibrated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:66
#: 1e77c367bfac4fa8a72a86d02103704f
msgid "Compasses should always be enabled for Copter/Rover, but may be disabled (not recommended, if one is available) for Plane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:69
#: ba1740efc3a24f1f868618cf872baab7
msgid "Orientation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:71
#: 193f41086f8842d6a7c6696f6a57f9ca
msgid "The :ref:`AHRS_ORIENTATION<AHRS_ORIENTATION>` must be set correctly for the compass calibration to be successful. In addition,the :ref:`common-accelerometer-calibration` should be completed before the Compass Calibration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:73
#: ff535f0267e14473898487a3759773e8
msgid "The setting of the orientation of external compasses is no longer required. It's determined automatically during :ref:`common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner` now. This can be disabled, or only report the orientation determined during Compass Calibration, using the :ref:`COMPASS_AUTO_ROT<COMPASS_AUTO_ROT>` parameter. The orientation determination CAN fail if the magnetic fields are compromised by nearby metal or other interference, especially on 45 deg offset orientations. If the compass is known to be mounted on a 45 degree bias to the accelerometers, and fails to determine orientation during the Compass Calibration, then setting :ref:`COMPASS_AUTO_ROT<COMPASS_AUTO_ROT>` to \"3\" and repeating the calibration, may yield a successful completion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:75
#: 4f18b81b7e6c4c0fa0b48d158b0fd59c
msgid "automatic determination of compass orientation ONLY occurs using normal Compass Calibration. :ref:`In-flight Calibration<automatic-compass-offset-calibration>` and :ref:`Large Vehicle Mag Calibration <large-vehicle-mag-cal>` require that the orientation be properly set BEFORE attempting these types of calibration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:77
#: 25beaae7ccdb417683fe44a7c1cc4a61
msgid "However, if the need to double-check the orientation of a compass should arise:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:79
#: 5c3bc7c466dd4643aafaeb4ba03df632
msgid "When rotating your aircraft through all axes each of the compasses should move in the same direction, and should be of approximately the same values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:81
#: 984c42d5d2034b3bad3d32147b84467b
msgid "Northern Hemisphere:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:82
#: 5e574ba5e046495f89c17080875d687f
msgid "Z-component should be *positive*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:83
#: 1907ee2eb75d47c8a610266a4f0bf2ef
msgid "when pitching the vehicle down, the X component should *increase* in value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:84
#: 541abf2eea60483e835eceecba3b4e9d
msgid "when rolling the vehicle right, the Y component should *increase* in value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:86
#: 9a65de8e4d7c4d4281413e5ad0ab8be4
msgid "Southern Hemisphere:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:87
#: 56f70a7253ba496491d0448d1cd33894
msgid "Z-component should be *negative*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:88
#: 1aa6c11ebbca4e2d9a907e36f10160b9
msgid "when pitching the vehicle down, the X component should *decrease* in value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:89
#: 4afd12bdf37045f3ac188157408f0d0f
msgid "when rolling the vehicle right, the Y component should *decrease* in value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:92
#: 0ae20ec456ca41bcbfde8c71d4d8ad11
msgid "Other parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:94
#: 63664d53305242898c7328c7e65e1ef3
msgid "Earlier versions of ArduPilot did not incorporate the world magnetic model database, and a locations magnetic declination might need to manually entered, or learned through flight. This is not necessary now. In addition, this allows the declination to be continuously updated on long distance flights."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:96
#: 985a7aaa5b2442389802ec559f07276b
msgid "Also, learning the compass offsets in flight, instead of ground calibration, is an option for vehicles difficult to move in order to calibrate. But is not recommended, since the Large Vehicle MagCal option is now available. See :ref:`common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner` page for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:104
#: 5675386dd31247b1aeca9d46b84b1bda
msgid "Automatic Offset Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:106
#: 5d869c98333540d9a1161c67a4cbeedd
msgid "DO NOT USE THIS WITH GPS-DERIVED YAW! ie :ref:`common-gps-for-yaw` in  firmware versions before 4.5.2!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:108
#: cb94b61014e8458cad1654a0ee81cee8
msgid "In the 4.0 and later releases of ArduPilot, an automatic offset learning feature is available. The :ref:`COMPASS_LEARN<COMPASS_LEARN>` parameter determines how this feature works. This is for advanced users and not recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:110
#: 7db5593da9d44ca58dee908cafc9c518
msgid "If set to 3, the offsets will be learned automatically during flight, be saved, and this parameter reset to 0. Position control modes (Loiter, Auto, etc.) should not be used while the offsets are being learned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:112
#: 067f620329c840d685e5c3572f8c2b0b
msgid "Setting :ref:`COMPASS_LEARN<COMPASS_LEARN>` to 1 or 2 is not recommended. These modes are deprecated and are either non-functional, or still in development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:114
#: b1b9ee7065f844078d1b4bbcc3b76075
msgid "The procedure for :ref:`COMPASS_LEARN<COMPASS_LEARN>` = 3 is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:116
#: d7891212cd8642159e1666e4d2b363b1
msgid "set :ref:`COMPASS_LEARN<COMPASS_LEARN>` = 3. The message “CompassLearn: Initialised” will appear on the MP’s message tab (it does not appear in red letters on the HUD)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:117
#: 8c2b19329fbd4ea8adc80b3d8386ee21
msgid "“Bad Compass” will appear but this is nothing to be worried about. We will hopefully make this disappear before the final release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:118
#: cca56eace6f1429c991043c178425d71
msgid "Arm and drive/fly the vehicle around in whatever mode you like, do some turns “CompassLearn: have earth field” should appear on MP’s message tab and then eventually “CompassLearn: finished”."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:120
#: 797b3f7ae4d649078366cd77c8092ace
msgid "You MUST have a GPS lock and signal for this to be successful. Be sure the GPS has a clear \"view\" of the sky and there are no obstructions blocking the GPS signals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:122
#: ed489ee6ca4d407ca05355b0fd17858a
msgid "If you want you can check the :ref:`COMPASS_LEARN<COMPASS_LEARN>` parameter has been set back to zero (you may need to refresh parameters to see this) and the COMPASS_OFS_X/Y/Z values will have changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:123
#: ed66131a58724b41a757bfa782bbe673
msgid "This method can also be evoked using the RCxOPTION for \"Compass Learn\". It will activate when the channel goes above 1800uS and automatically complete and save."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:128
#: b9d73e0d78994a3baabe11629e4c82f9
msgid "Compass error messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:130
#: 908c1868c9c243c5ade412e76c888a70
msgid "**Compass Health**: The compass has not sent a signal for at least half a second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:132
#: 9fb3ccf352f64597910b5dd4cad35d72
msgid "**Compass Variance**: In the EKF solution, compass heading disagrees with the heading estimate from other inertial sensors. Clicking the EKF button on the Mission Planner HUD will show the magnitude of the error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:136
#: 40fdb8bd38894ffb9c156e1d0f4a7143
msgid "**Compass Not Calibrated**: The compass needs to be calibrated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:137
#: 6e8ce86aadd941239909fa02183212bc
msgid "**Compass Offsets High**: One of your compass offsets exceeds 600, indicating likely magnetic interference. Check for sources of interference and try calibrating again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:142
#: 585fa8f4b4a6486aaa192bc8ce154f64
msgid "Refining Calibration Parameters using a Flight Log"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:144
#: a2b3b0f78d004063b95e8de82b8e718b
msgid "The compass offsets, scales, diagonals, and even motor compensation can be determined from a flight dataflash log of the vehicle using an analysis utility."
msgstr ""
